From 332df18e67c0f689d4dd5d0b2154e612cd871b3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Mirchev <mmirchev@comp.nus.edu.sg>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:45:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: reject tfra boxes smaller than their header

mov_read_mfra() calls read_tfra() until it returns non-zero, and
read_tfra() ends by seeking to the box start plus its declared size.
A tfra box with size 0 therefore seeks back onto itself and is parsed
again forever. Since the whole box stays in the AVIOContext buffer, no
read reaches the protocol layer and the interrupt callback is never
checked, so the demuxer cannot be interrupted either.

The mfra is read on the first moof when use_mfra_for is enabled, which
an "Anevia" free box does by default, so a 76-byte file can make
avformat_open_input() spin indefinitely.

Signed-off-by: Martin Mirchev <mmirchev@comp.nus.edu.sg>
(cherry picked from commit 332df18e67c0f689d4dd5d0b2154e612cd871b3e)
---
 libavformat/mov.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
index 649d8d20518b..d2aafaaac716 100644
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -10516,6 +10516,12 @@ static int read_tfra(MOVContext *mov, AVIOContext *f)
     if (avio_rb32(f) != MKBETAG('t', 'f', 'r', 'a')) {
         return 1;
     }
+    /* A tfra box can not be smaller than its 24-byte header. A size of 0
+     * would make mov_read_mfra() re-read the same box forever. */
+    if (size < 24) {
+        av_log(mov->fc, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Invalid tfra size %"PRIu32"\n", size);
+        return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
+    }
     av_log(mov->fc, AV_LOG_VERBOSE, "found tfra\n");
 
     version = avio_r8(f);
